  message: "Rolled up under class item INV-linub-nokij-gibim-rovok-moros-gural-domip-rimof (filed 2026-08-06), which now holds isbefore on this item. NOT a duplicate finding: the class exists because three per-analyzer items share one invariant, and because reading _match_propagation_entry / _lookup_named_entry showed the chain has FOUR links, not one. Emission (L2) is where these items sit; receiver evidence (L3) and the io-boundary F3 gate (L4) are downstream and can refuse an edge that emission successfully adds. So a fix scoped to emission alone can move zero findings while looking like a win at the analyzer. Do not start a fix here until the class measurement fills go/rust/objc and reads the declining branch in each failing analyzer."  # 71ab
- op: discuss  # a09e
  at: '2026-08-06T05:08:44Z'  # a09e
  by: agent  # a09e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a09e
  clock: 3  # a09e
  nonce: a09e  # a09e
  message: "CORRECTION to this item published table, 2026-08-06, from an independent re-measurement (meas/chain_probe.py + meas/fixtures/, one instrument, production _match_propagation_entry). The EMISSION column reproduces exactly - java/scala/swift emit in both forms, python emits two-step only, kotlin and javascript emit neither. That half stands and the re-measurement confirms it. The column header EMITS + MATCHES does not: java, scala, swift and python two-step all EMIT and DO NOT MATCH. Their edges carry module hint external and call_construct method, and io_boundary.gate_named_entry opens with an unconditional if call_construct == method: return None. This was already visible in this campaign own prior artifact makij_match3.txt, which recorded python:external:0-0:decrypt:unresolved -> None on a different fixture. So the matching claim was never established for any language; the header conflated it with emission. Kotlin note for the record: an earlier draft of my probe appeared to contradict this item by reporting kotlin emits. It was MY probe that was wrong - it attributed the File(path) CONSTRUCTOR edge to the method site. This item was right. Corrected probe agrees: kotlin emits nothing for writeText in either form."  # a09e
