  clock: 10  # 9a99
  nonce: 9a99  # 9a99
  message: "JAVASCRIPT CELL CLOSED, PR #753 (dev 82a973b69f): an instance-method call on an\nuntyped receiver -- a bare name or ANY receiver expression nothing typed\n(`f().m()`, `a[i].m()`, an inline `new` of an unknown class; `this` keeps\nSite 1) -- emits `javascript:external:0-0:<method>:unresolved` with\n`call_construct: method` (parity with python/java/go/rust/scala/swift); a\n`new`-constructed receiver carries its constructor's module (INV-misup, same\nPR). This item's own fixture -- `helper(x)`, `fs.readFileSync(x)`,\n`console.log(x)` emitting and `obj.write(x)` not -- now emits all four\n(`test_obj_write_emits_beside_its_siblings`). Per the owner's 2026-08-23\nruling, `analyzer_disclosure` flips javascript's dated declaration rather than\nan invariant turning red; a clean verdict now carries `untyped_receiver`\ndisclosures per site instead of `analyzer_method_call_blind`. Recall claim:\nNONE for the untyped shape (an `external` placeholder reaches no row --\npinned `_tagged == 0`); the constructed shape is where rows are reached.\nMEASURED: per call site, both arms in one process: mobx 15,188 -> 35,743 sites, plausible 3,054 -> 5,244 (5 XMLHttpRequest typed), workadventure 25,116 -> 54,672 (35 XMLHttpRequest + 8 WebSocket typed), 0 sites lost a type; plausible's one resolved->typed site is `xhr.open` leaving a wrong short-name in-repo binding for XMLHttpRequest.open. io-boundaries: mobx 60 -> 60, plausible 54 -> 59 (+5, all XMLHttpRequest egress, every site read back), workadventure 60 -> 78 (+17 XMLHttpRequest in Emscripten's doXHR loader inside minified wasm glue, +1 BroadcastChannel.postMessage in a service worker); 0 chains lost.\nKOTLIN CELL STILL OPEN -- next PR: rig `nasuf_kotlin_09032026/`, arm A\nokhttp 49 chains (all println) / detekt 2 chains (both println), 0 method-kind.\nRUST cell (this thread, 2026-08-23: `sock.send(payload)` on an annotated\n`&UdpSocket` param emits nothing) NOT touched here."  # 9a99
