- op: discuss  # 6f5f
  at: '2026-09-04T03:02:51Z'  # 6f5f
  by: agent  # 6f5f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6f5f
  clock: 12  # 6f5f
  nonce: 6f5f  # 6f5f
  message: "KOTLIN CELL CLOSED, PR #755 (dev 2cffc262d2). Mechanism as read on 2026-09-03:\nCase 3 (typed receiver), 3b (extension) and 4 (qualified fallback) were ALL gated\non `resolver.lookup(...).found`, and nothing emitted otherwise -- and `val c:\nConnection = make()` never read its declared type at all. Now: `_kt_declared_type`\nbinds a declared local; `_kt_constructor_type` types a bare or dotted constructor\n(`java.io.File(p)`) and a CHAINED receiver (`File(p).writeText(s)`, a\ncall_expression receiver the branch never captured); after Case 4 misses,\n`make_unresolved_edge(\"kotlin\", ..., module_hint=_kt_receiver_module(type,\nimports) or \"external\", receiver_type_hint=type, call_construct=\"method\")`.\n`_kt_receiver_module`: import | inline dotted path (lowercase head) | nested on an\nimported outer; a bare unimported name is LEFT ALONE (no implicit-package guess --\nkotlin auto-imports kotlin.* / kotlin.io.* / java.lang.*, and the catalogue's rows\nare explicitly imported JDK types, so a closed list buys nothing yet; recorded as\nthe re-evaluation trigger). `analyzer_disclosure` kotlin flipped (dated).\nTwo defects the per-site read-back on okhttp found in the fix itself, both fixed and pinned before the PR: kotlin keys a nested class's methods by the INNER class (`Builder.url`), so a receiver typed by its dotted constructor (`Request.Builder()`) missed the in-repo lookup a bare `Builder` hits -- 146 sites went resolved -> unresolved until `_kt_project_type_key` normalised the lookup and the linker hint; and `var_types` was file-scoped, so `var factory: LoggingEventListener.Factory` in one method retyped the class FIELD `factory` used in a later one (a present-but-wrong module in the slot) -- locals now close with their function, the java INV-vugon rule. A third: the old ctor typing walked into a call CHAIN and typed the local from its ROOT (`val r = MockResponse().setBody(x)`, `val s = Cfg(..).subConfig(\"a\")`); requiring the outermost callee to be the constructor lost 95 resolved sites, so `_kt_chain_root_constructor` keeps the root as the evidence -- a builder's true return type is WI-lalot's, and no better evidence exists here. And a fourth, one pass later: a DOTTED constructor at the root of a LONGER chain (`val request = Request.Builder().url(u).build()`) types the local as the OUTER class (`Request`), which the old arm did and `.build()` returns; the precise `Request.Builder` is right only when the constructor is the whole initializer -- 89 `request.tag()` sites had gone unresolved. And a fifth: okhttp writes builder chains one segment per line, and a constructor test that read the navigation text with its newlines failed `isidentifier()` on every segment -- 89 sites; the segments are the evidence, the whitespace is not.\nMEASURED: io-boundaries okhttp 49 -> 52 (socket.connect x2 net_send, logFile.appendText fs_write), detekt 2 -> 6 (Path.inputStream / bufferedWriter / toFile, File.writer); every new chain read back against source; 0 lost. Per call site, both arms in one process: okhttp 22,196 -> 46,555 sites, 4,527 typed gains, 0 re-keys, 8 sites lost a resolution: 4 are a wrong short-name in-repo bind on LinkedHashSet.add corrected to the JDK type, 4 are a class field initialised by a lowercase factory (`val clientTestRule = configureClientTestRule()`) that the old arm typed only through a same-named LOCAL leaking out of another function; detekt 12,724 -> 27,172 sites, 5,041 typed gains, 1 lost (the same leak shape, `gradleRunner`).\nSTILL OPEN under this item: the RUST cell (2026-08-23 note: `sock.send(payload)`\non an annotated `&UdpSocket` parameter emits nothing) -- not touched by the three\nPRs (java #750 / python #752 / javascript #753 / kotlin #755); file or\nre-scope this item to rust once the owner's queue is done.\n\nCI false-red on the first push (#755): the changed-file coverage gate reported kotlin.py:1027-1073 (the WI-dorop enum_entry loop, not this PR's code) uncovered. That block is covered solely by test_scala_cpp_kotlin_enum_members.py, which reaches the analyzer through the registry (`run_analyzer(\"kotlin\", ...)`) and imports nothing, so the import-graph slice never selected it. Fixed structurally through the WI-zaziz map (.ci/coverage-only-deps.txt): kotlin.py, scala.py and cpp.py now each name that test, so the regenerated manifest carries it on every future change to any of the three."  # 6f5f
